        "id": 1279898
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-21T23:42:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am indeed! You may be interested in b/281589918 where I\u0027m dumping some more findings, I\u0027ve also found a hangup here in ServiceConnector where the timeout task isn\u0027t getting processed: aosp/2629381. The fix in Watchdog you\u0027ve found also seems relevant to the problem at hand.",
      "parentUuid": "d2d1a757_382eb97a",
      "revId": "0cb9c2c57a0860deed5df6b9b11e6423f8e325ab",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47222e79_930e458b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 2009035
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-22T00:46:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately, I don\u0027t have permission to access that bug report. I got far enough to note that PermissionPolicyService blocks system_server\u0027s main thread inside ActivityManagerService#systemReady, but the future cannot complete until ActivityManagerService#finishBooting is called. It seemed like a deadlock, not directly related to any timeout. Once I found a workaround, though, I did not dig further.\n\nI will see what effect aosp/2629381 has, and I\u0027m happy to test anything else that might remove the need for the workaround.",
      "parentUuid": "9018a6d8_5a71a0a3",
      "revId": "0cb9c2c57a0860deed5df6b9b11e6423f8e325ab",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "667aeb3e_22afeccf",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1279898
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-22T14:45:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, apologies - roughly what that bug finds is that there\u0027s other issues occurring in PermissionControllerManager:\n\n1) aosp/2629749, within PCM we\u0027re not honoring the hardware boot multiplier, so we\u0027re often not giving enough time for default grants to be applied.\n2) aosp/2629381, occasionally when it takes too long, the system should at least recover by restarting zygote, but it currently doesn\u0027t - this CL fixes an issue where we block the main thread and never run the timeout handler.",
      "parentUuid": "47222e79_930e458b",
      "revId": "0cb9c2c57a0860deed5df6b9b11e6423f8e325ab",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
